# SAHW machine config — copy this to .env and fill in for this box.
#
# .env is gitignored; this file (.env.example) is the committed shape. The server reads .env once,
# before it builds its own defaults, and fills only the variables it does not already have in the
# environment — so a value you export in the shell, or pass as a flag, always wins.
#
# The values shown are the shipped fallbacks: loopback, the UI's own port, and the two SAH locations
# left silent. Name this machine's real ones.

# --- what the UI lists --------------------------------------------------------
# The folder holding the run folders — SAH's runs root, written by `--runs-root` on every launch. The
# tree the UI shows is derived from each run's own log, so one root holds every workspace's runs.
# Shipped fallback is silent: the UI lists and streams the logs it can read, and a spawn is refused
# with the line that names it. Set this box's runs root.
#SAHW_RUNS_ROOT=

# --- what the UI launches -----------------------------------------------------
# The SAH tree a spawned run runs from: its `.venv` holds the interpreter and `PYTHONPATH` is set to
# this folder, because the package runs from source and the run's working directory is the workspace it
# was started in. Shipped fallback is silent: the UI still lists and streams the logs it can read, and
# POST /api/runs refuses with the flag that names it. Set this box's SAH tree.
#SAHW_SAH_TREE=

# --- the port -----------------------------------------------------------------
# The port the UI answers on. Loopback is the only address the server listens on: it has no auth, and a
# workspace browser on a reachable interface is a share of the machine. Shipped fallback: 8321.
SAHW_PORT=8321

# --- the open act --------------------------------------------------------------
# Set to 1 to keep the server from opening folders and files on the machine: the open acts then refuse
# with the line that names it (a headless box, or a verification that must not open windows). Shipped
# fallback: unset — the server opens, the way an operator's own machine owes it.
#SAHW_NO_OPEN=

# --- the stream's pace ----------------------------------------------------------
# How often a followed run's stream asks its log whether it grew, in seconds. The run's trace — the
# words as they arrive — is drained once per that look, so this is the pace the live pane fills: a
# lower value fills it sooner, at the cost of a file asked more often. Shipped fallback: 0.02.
#SAHW_STREAM_POLL=
